{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Cloven-hoofed.</b> Split, as the Targum renders." "<b>Hoof.</b> פלאנט\"א." "<b>And wholly split.</b> Divided into two claws — for there is one that is split but not divided in the claws, and it is unclean." "<b>Among the beast.</b> The verse implies: whatever is found in the beast you may eat. From here they said that the fetus is permitted by the slaughter of its mother (Ḥullin 69)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {1 "the la'az is Old French plante, 'sole of the foot / hoof'"}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:47:00.649600919Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}